    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/3414/0/461120/889/cleaners-mc1229": {
      "title": "Cleaners",
      "description": "Cleaners - MC1229 Register Login Back to search results Cleaners - MC1229 We are looking for cleaners to join the Support\nServices team in Estates. You should have knowledge and experience of\ncleaning practices, products and equipment and the ability to cope well when\nunder pressure and demonstrate trustworthiness, dependability and initiative,\nalong with an enthusiastic and helpful manner. Current hours available : 15 hours per week, Monday to Friday:   06:00 - 09:00 10 hours per week, Monday - Friday: 0600-0800 20 hours per week, Monday to Friday: 0600-1000 12 hours per week, Saturday and Sunday: 06:00-12:00 8 hours per week, Saturday and Sunday: 14:00-18:00 Experience in a similar environment is\ndesirable, but training will be given. Please indicate on your application form\nwhich vacancy you are applying for. Further information and informal enquiries\nmay be directed to Cleaning Supervisors Tel: 01334 462333 Applications should consist of (please delete as required): ·         Letter of application (to include to include which post you are applying for). ·         CV ·         Names and contacts of two referees Employees of the University\nhave access to a wide range of staff benefits\nincluding: ·        \nAnnual leave of 30 days, plus 5 public holidays pro rata ·        \nFinancial contribution to relocation where applicable ·        \nMembership of the S&LAS Pension Scheme with generous employer\ncontributions ·        \nA hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where\nappropriate and a range of family friendly policies ·        \nStaff discount scheme for local and national goods and services ·        \nFree staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and\nsubsidised local bus travel ·        \nSubsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes\nfor staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn\nLearning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme Applications are\nparticularly welcome from, people from the Black, Asian and Minority Ethnic\n(BAME) community, and other protected characteristics who are under-represented\nin professional posts at the University. At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we\nare and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to\ncreating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our\nparticipation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan,\nCarer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. \nWe particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian,\nminority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled\npeople. This role is not eligible for visa sponsorship.  Information on\nother visa options is available at https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa or by contacting our HR Immigration Team on hrimmigration@st-andrews.ac.uk. Job description - MC1229RH FPs.pdf Estates Start date: As soon as possible Salary: £25,353 per annum pro rata Apply now Back to search results Cleaners - MC1229 School/Unit: Estates Posted: 02/12/2025 Closing Date: Ongoing Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the