    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/1041/0/475086/889/research-assistant-ar3345": {
      "title": "Research Assistant",
      "description": "Research Assistant - AR3345 Register Login Back to search results Research Assistant - AR3345 Applications are sought for a committed Research Assistant to work with Dr Lizzie Bradford and Dr Kimberly More conducting research for an Experimental Psychology Society (EPS) funded project entitled Food Choice: The Collaborative Roles of Executive (Dys)Function and Identity.  The primary duties will be to oversee recruitment of participants (young adults/students), actively engage in data collection, support research activities related to the project, assist with data processing, and oversee and train project volunteers, under the supervision of Dr Lizzie Bradford and Dr Kimberly More. The successful applicant will have a background in Psychology or related field (e.g., undergraduate degree) with experience in data collection with in-person human participants. The post is available for 26 weeks (6.5 months) starting in November 2026 or as soon as possible thereafter. Applications should be submitted via email to eefb@st-andrews.ac.uk and krm24@st-andrews.ac.uk by 5pm (UK time) on Wednesday 14th October 2026. If you are applying through redeployment, please also make us aware via email to vacancies@st-andrews.ac.uk. For further information and informal enquiries, please contact Dr Lizzie Bradford at eefb@st-andrews.ac.uk or Dr Kimberly More at krm24@st-andrews.ac.uk In addition to the salary on offer for this position, there are a wide\nrange of benefits for staff working at the University of St Andrews. Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with a generous\n    employer contribution of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial\n    homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies,\n    supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and\n    services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to\n    Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on\n    degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities\n    including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice\n    scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays (pro rata). At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. This role is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Information on other visa options is available at https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa or by contacting our HR Immigration Team on hrimmigration@st-andrews.ac.uk. Closing date: 14 October 2026 Interview date: 21 October 2026 Job description: AR3345RS FPs.pdf Ref no: AR3345RS School of Psychology & Neuroscience Salary: Grade 5 / £32,080 pa pro rata Start date: 2 November 2026 Part time: 7 hours per week Fixed term: 26 weeks Back to search results Research Assistant - AR3345 School/Unit: School of Psychology & Neuroscience Posted: 02/10/2026 Closing date: 14/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/3468/0/474508/889/clinical-evidence-fellow-ar3333": {
      "title": "Clinical Evidence Fellow",
      "description": "Clinical Evidence Fellow - AR3333 Register Login Back to search results Clinical Evidence Fellow - AR3333 Applications are sought for a Clinical Research Fellow to work with Dr Margaret McCartney and Professor Frank Sullivan, and Prof. Fergus Daly in the School of Medicine as well as Dr. Dhairini  Balasubramaniam in the School of Computer Science and Prof Linda Bauld (University of Edinburgh) conducting research funded by Public Health Scotland: Social Media Made Better for Health Emergencies. The primary duties will be to use the findings from systematic reviews on health communications and to assist in the development of creating a method to create reliable, evidence based information packages in response to health stories or trending topics on social media, and helping with preliminary testing. Successful applicants will have a passion for evidence based healthcare, critical appraisal, and public communication about healthcare issues. They will also have research skills, particularly experience in systematic reviews. Applicants for this position should be broadly experienced clinicians working in clinical practice. This 0.1 FTE post is available from February 2027 for six months in the 1 st instance. For further information and informal enquiries, please contact Dr Margaret McCartney at mm494@st-andrews.ac.uk In addition to the salary on offer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St Andrews: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with a generous employer contribution of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays (pro rata). At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. This role is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Information on other visa options is available at https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa or by contacting our HR Immigration Team on hrimmigration@st-andrews.ac.uk. Closing date: 15 October 2026 Interview date: 29 October 2026 Job description: AR3333LS FPs.pdf Ref no: AR3333LS School of Medicine Salary: Clinical Pay Scale (to be negotiated) Start date: February 2027 Part time: 0.1 FTE Fixed term: 6 months Apply now Back to search results Clinical Evidence Fellow - AR3333 School/Unit: School of Medicine Posted: 17/09/2026 Closing date: 15/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5906/0/475121/889/placement-administrator-cg2292": {
      "title": "Placement Administrator",
      "description": "Placement Administrator - CG2292 Register Login Back to search results Placement Administrator - CG2292 We are seeking to appoint an\nenthusiastic and organised Placement Administrator to join the School of\nMedicine's teaching support team. Working closely with the placement group,\nacademic colleagues, students, and our NHS partners, the post holder will help\nsupport the effective delivery of high-quality placement experiences across all\nour undergraduate medical programmes. The Placement Administrator\nwill contribute to a collaborative team responsible for the planning,\ncoordination, and administration of student placements across a range of\nproviders. The role will focus on maintaining accurate records, ensuring that\nadministrative processes are delivered effectively while supporting\ncommunication with placement providers to help build and maintain strong\nworking relationships. The role requires attention\nto detail, high level of accuracy and the ability to manage multiple priorities\nwithin a busy and complex environment. The School of Medicine is\ncommitted to continuous improvement and innovation in its administrative\npractices. We are therefore looking for an individual with strong digital\nskills who is keen to identify opportunities to streamline processes, improve\ndocument management and make effective use of technology and automation to\nenhance service delivery. Enquiries can be directed to\nCaroline Forbes, Teaching Operations Manager medteachingmanager@st-andrews.ac.uk or Katie Jardine, Placements and MedSupport Group Lead katie.jardine@st-andrews.ac.uk St Andrews offers more than just a place to work it is\na place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are\ncommitted to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their\nbest. In addition to the salary on offer for this position,\nthere are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St\nAndrews. The package for the Placement Administrator includes: Financial contribution to relocation (subject\n    to eligibility) Membership of the S&LAS Pension Scheme with\n    generous employer contributions A hybrid working environment, including partial\n    homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies,\n    supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and\n    services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to\n    Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on\n    degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities\n    including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice\n    scheme 30 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality,\ndiversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of\nour University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and\nsupportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters\nand awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality\nCharter. We particularly welcome\napplications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority\nreligions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people Closing Date 15 October 2026 Interview Date 22 October 2026 Please quote ref: CG2292LS Job Description: CG2292LSFPs.pdf School of Medicine Salary: £25,353 - £26,707 per annum Start Date 01 November 2026 Apply now Back to search results Placement Administrator - CG2292 School/Unit: School of Medicine Posted: 02/10/2026 Closing date: 15/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be 