    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/3647/0/475306/889/information-analyst-accreditation-ad2923": {
      "title": "Information Analyst (Accreditation)",
      "description": "Information Analyst (Accreditation) - AD2923 Register Login Back to search results Information Analyst (Accreditation) - AD2923 The University of St Andrews is seeking an analytical, curious and highly motivated Information Analyst (Accreditation) to join its Planning Unit, someone who enjoys solving complex problems using data and can communicate findings clearly to a wide range of audiences. This is a unique opportunity to combine data analysis, business intelligence, reporting, project support and strategic insight within a role that directly contributes to the success and reputation of a world-renowned institution. Working within a collaborative team of analytical professionals, you will play a key role in supporting the Business School's prestigious international accreditation activities, helping to deliver the evidence, reporting and insights required for accreditation frameworks including EQUIS, AMBA and AACSB. This is far more than a traditional reporting position. You will have the opportunity to: Lead the production of high-quality management information, data analysis, reports and visualisations that support major accreditation activities. Develop and maintain specialist datasets, evidence repositories and data assets that underpin strategic decision-making. Design dashboards and analytical outputs that transform complex information into clear, actionable insight. Work with senior leaders, professional services colleagues and academic staff across the University. Support a diverse portfolio of analytical work spanning student recruitment, league tables, graduate outcomes, equality and diversity, sustainability, finance and institutional performance. No two days are the same. You'll work on challenges that influence strategic planning, institutional success and the experience of students and staff across the University. Employees of the University have access to a wide range of staff benefits including: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the S&LAS Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. This post will be primarily based at the Eden Campus at Guardbridge, a state-of-the-art working environment for professional services units. Further information and informal enquiries may be directed to Jonathan McDougall Bagnall, email: jmb15@st-andrews.ac.uk . At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. This role is not eligible for visa sponsorship.  Information on other visa options is available at https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa or by contacting our HR Immigration Team on hrimmigration@st-andrews.ac.uk . Closing Date: 23 October 2026 Interview Date: 4 November 2026 Please quote ref: AD2923SB Job Description: AD2923SB FPs.pdf Planning Salary: £32,080 - £37,694 per annum Start: As soon as possible Apply now Back to search results Information Analyst (Accreditation) - AD2923 School/Unit: Planning Posted: 07/10/2026 Closing date: 23/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter ⚡ by Freshworks 1"
