    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/4787/0/473304/889/associate-lecturer-in-organic-chemistry-education-focused-aoac7905rx": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer in Organic Chemistry (Education Focused)",
      "description": "Associate Lecturer in Organic Chemistry (Education Focused) - AOAC7905RX Register Login Back to search results Associate Lecturer in Organic Chemistry (Education Focused) - AOAC7905RX The School of Chemistry invites applications\nfor the position of Associate Lecturer in Organic Chemistry (Education\nFocused). This is a fixed-term position for 12 months to cover a period of\nstaff research leave. Applicants will have a PhD in Chemistry and,\nideally, previous teaching experience in the field of Organic Chemistry. The successful applicant\nwill deliver teaching to undergraduate in organic chemistry and there may be\nopportunities to contribute to postgraduate courses.  In addition, the successful candidate will\nassess student work and progress and provide constructive feedback and\ncontribute to the delivery of the undergraduate programme in Chemistry. St Andrews offers more than just a place to work it is\na place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are\ncommitted to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their\nbest. In addition to the salary on offer for this position,\nthere are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St\nAndrews. The package for the Associate Lecturer in Organic Chemistry includes: Financial contribution to relocation (subject\n    to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with a generous\n    employer contribution of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial\n    homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies,\n    supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and\n    services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to\n    Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on\n    degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities\n    including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice\n    scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality,\ndiversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of\nour University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and\nsupportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters\nand awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality\nCharter. We particularly welcome\napplications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority\nreligions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. Closing Date: 27 November 2026 Interview Date: 21 January 2027 Please quote ref: AOAC7905RX Job Description: AOAC7905RXFPs.pdf School of Chemistry Salary: £38,784 - £44,746 per annum Fixed Term for 12 months Apply now Back to search results Associate Lecturer in Organic Chemistry (Education Focused) - AOAC7905RX School/Unit: School of Chemistry Posted: 24/08/2026 Closing date: 27/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
